From 985f4630cb8144529135d5ef93649af0680ced4a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 14:01:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 01/16] Engine compatibility ranges (gap rank 5): lineage,
 engine.migrated, one-way resume

src/engine-lineage.json (in the engine identity) declares this engine's version (2), the
oldest version whose runs it resumes (1) and each predecessor's exact file map. A recorded
engine hash is recognised only when that map plus this host's platform fields hashes to it.
Runtime.execute resumes such a run and commits engine.migrated with runner.acquired,
moving the record's engineHash by compare-and-swap; anything else is ENGINE_DRIFT, and an
older engine refuses a migrated run. engineBinding(events) is the chain's engine for the
runtime, identityChanges and verify-run (ENGINE_MIGRATED, ENGINE_MIGRATION_INVALID).
Version 1 = commit 96cab64 (hash 358cb020... on node v24.21.0/linux/x64/ajv 8.20.0).
Design: research/engine-20261021/ENGINE-BUMP.md section 1. tools/engine-lineage.mjs prints
the entry to freeze at the next release.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
